ios: music loops

A song played once and then the music stopped until the server sent a different one: the server sends a song only on
entering a map square whose song is another (music_playbyregion), the client drops a MIDI_SONG of the song it has, and
upstream's tinymidipcm left looping out (commented out in flush: "buggy with some midi files"). Only the music tab's
Loop, off again at every login (musicloop is a temp varp), sent the song again: silence and the song, a 7 s fade over
nothing, then the song from its start.

A song now loops in the player: once it has all been rendered and flushed and less than 2 s of it are left to play,
flush() has it rendered again from its first message (TinyMidiPCM.replay(): no second parse, whose messages the wasm
could not free), its buffers queued right after the last one. A jingle still plays once: the client plays every song
with a fade and only a jingle without, and its nextMusicDelay brings the song back after it. The song that is playing
and looping, sent again (only Loop does that), keeps playing instead of fading out and restarting.

Music off, logout and a new song stop the loop as they stopped a song (stop(): flush no longer runs; start() clears
it). The render, the buffers and their timing are as before.

